File Index

/App.css
Purpose: Every auc-* class — rebuilt in A2 on index.css's C#-derived design tokens: panel cards, pill nav with the blue→orange header underline, striped rounded admin table, chip buttons with warm hover. Class names unchanged from Phase 1 (pages/tests depend on them); :has(.auc-page--wide) widens the shell for the admin tables.

/App.test.tsx
Purpose: A2 Admin-tab visibility off me().globalRole — hidden for 'user', shown for an elevated tier (the API enforces regardless). Phase B: /signup pathname lands on the signup form; any other pathname still defaults to login.

/App.tsx
Purpose: The whole app's routing — switches on useAuthSession()'s status between the public flows (login/signup/forgot-password), ForcedChangePage, and the logged-in shell (account / "Keys & devices" / admin nav — devices live INSIDE the keys section, see features/devices/.annotated for why); also parses /reset-password?token=... and /verify-email?token=... off window.location once on mount to hand the right page its landing token. Phase A: /sso/authorize renders SsoApprovePage INSTEAD of the shell once the session is ready — login/forced-change still run first, so consent always happens on a fully-onboarded session; malformed params keep the branch active so the error card renders rather than the account shell. A2: an Admin tab appears only when me().globalRole isn't 'user' (server enforces regardless). Phase B: /signup is a landing pathname that defaults publicView to the signup form instead of login — added so a consumer's own Register action (DSL's shatteredarchive.com) can send new visitors somewhere that isn't a sign-IN screen (a real bug caught live 2026-07-27: redirecting to the hub root landed everyone on Login).

/index.css
Purpose: A2 design-token home — CSS custom properties extracted (grep-verified) from the C# site's site.css: dark neutrals, #6f93ff/#f19a47 accents, #1D94E4 link hover, radii/shadows/mono stack. The constellation's reference identity style; App.css consumes these.

/main.tsx
Purpose: Standard createRoot/StrictMode bootstrap.
